    <!-- Haven round 12, launcher icon ONLY. User-approved
         reference (2026-11-04, "Use this, build it as round
         12"): the layered preview image (imagine_media/
         media-generation-haven-icon-layered-preview-0-...
         webp) — cream squircle field, house whose green roof
         blends through a warm golden center, pale arched
         door on the LEFT, bottom split light green (left) +
         green (right), yellow sparkle upper right, and NO
         dark green curved band sweeping from the top left,
         NO dark rectangle at the bottom center.
         CONSTRUCTION — A SERIES OF LAYERED SEMI-OPAQUE
         POLYGONS (the user's words, 2026-11-04). Round 10's
         error was tracing the reference as SOLID FLAT OPAQUE
         facets: on device it read as hard flat shapes, not
         the reference's depth. Here every layer except the
         shell and the sparkle carries android:fillAlpha < 1,
         stacked bottom-to-top so the OVERLAPS create the
         blends (golden center over green shell, bright roof
         over shell, lime over shell) instead of hard opaque
         color boundaries. The layer stack, bottom to top:
           L1 shell        #3FA85E alpha 1.00 (full house)
           L2 roof         #8EE059 alpha 0.55 (roof polygon)
           L3 golden band  #E8B93B alpha 0.78 (broad band)
           L4 golden core  #F5C542 alpha 0.55 (inner blob)
           L5 door         #F0D67E alpha 0.92 (pale arch, LEFT)
           L6 bottom wash  #8EE059 alpha 0.35 (full-width bottom)
           L7 bottom lime  #8EE059 alpha 0.85 (bottom-left)
           L8 bottom teal  #1E7A4C alpha 0.25 (bottom from x=56)
           L9 bottom teal  #1E7A4C alpha 0.30 (bottom from x=68)
           L10 sparkle     #F8C230 alpha 1.00 (star)
           L11 sparkle pale #FFFBEA alpha 0.55 (pale quadrant)
         No layer is dark enough, and no overlap lands, where
         the removed dark band or dark bottom block were: the
         bottom center below the band is shell green with the
         lime/shade split at x=46, exactly as in the preview.
         HARD CONSTRAINTS (device history):
         - ZERO <gradient> elements. Round 7 proved the Fold8
           adaptive-icon path does not render gradient-filled
           vector paths (the house vanished; only the solid
           sparkle rendered). Alpha fills are NOT gradients
           and are used here instead.
         - fillAlpha is UNPROVEN on that same path: it may
           honor translucency, or it may flatten layers to
           opaque (which would read close to round 10 again).
           Only the user's device test (grid vs recents) can
           settle it; this file claims nothing about it.
         GEOMETRY (same safe envelope as rounds 7/9/10, house
         within 30..78 x 26..76, sparkle inside the 66dp safe
         circle): shell, roof, band, door, and sparkle reuse
         the round-10 coordinates, so the monochrome variant
         (same silhouette + evenOdd door cutout + sparkle)
         is unchanged. Background (cream field) unchanged.
         Legacy PNGs are rasterized from THIS file (see
         make-legacy-icon-round12.py), so they match the
         vector layer for layer. -->
